{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790175578,"nonce":"sKAl65xdtvTp2ycfsJ+Ki5CSWtU=","title":"Nested native enum getters can lazily install another published Wren class while the interpreter is still evaluating an expression. Reproduction: the window-events plugin, import only window:Samples, then System.print(Samples.event(2).force.force). Depending on module-table allocation, the interpreter segfaults or reports that Null does not implement print(_).","message":"The interpreter caches pointers into engine.modules and a Vec header for an entire dispatch loop. A reentrant interpret_bytecode call can grow that HashMap without restarting the caller loop. Its cached pointers then address freed/moved entries.\n\nLocal fix uses the existing separately allocated ModuleVarsCell for reads and ordinary writes; growing a variable vector looks up the current module entry and synchronizes the cell. No per-access HashMap lookup is added to the common path. Regression: tests/reentrant_module.rs installs 64 modules from a host method and checks caller reads/writes. Caribou's plugin_window_events_wren additionally exercises nested enums, file bytes and scale callbacks.\n\nThe fix is isolated in sibling worktree ../wren_lift-caribou-events at Caribou's pinned 631db68 revision. The main ../wren_lift checkout has unrelated newer ABI changes and is unchanged. Caribou has a temporary Cargo patch to this worktree. Upstream publication and replacing the path patch remain pending.","files":null}]}